    {"area": "Practice", "checked": "2026-11-24", "point": "The protocol still tells a firm to give a 7-day cancellation notice under the Cancellation of Contracts Regulations 2008. Those regulations were revoked. An off-premises or distance contract is now covered by the Consumer Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013, which give 14 days. A signed retainer may ask the firm to start every section during those 14 days. It cannot waive the right on signature. Regulation 36: the right to cancel a section ends only when that section has been fully performed. Until then the client pays a reasonable amount for the work already done if they cancel. A contract made at the firm’s office is not given that right.", "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2013/3134/regulation/36"},
